{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/920964-sidereal-wfhl-armed-and-armored-in-starlight-shieldbreaker","id":920964,"title":"[Sidereal:WFHL] Armed and Armored in Starlight - Shieldbreaker","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-25T08:16:47-07:00","id":920964,"title":"[Sidereal:WFHL] Armed and Armored in Starlight - Shieldbreaker","content":"<b>Shieldbreaker (Orihalcum and Starmetal Grand Goremaul, Artifact oooo)</b><br /> <br /> One of the Thirteen Final Weapons, Shieldbreaker was forged by the Chosen of Battles Implacable Will near the end of the wars against the ancient Larmidian people in what would become the Ciner Isles, during the early years of the First Age. It was carried into battle by the Lawgiver Anyung, and was placed in her tomb after her death during the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> During Anyung\u2019s life, she became known as the Gracefully Descending Doom. Shieldbreaker was an utterly irresistible force, crushing through fortress walls and hard steel shields both as if they were no more than paper. She was especially noted for hurling the giant weapon up, allowing its massive bulk to carry her skyward and then guiding it with the force of a falling star onto her hapless foes.<br /> <br /> Shieldbreaker is a sphere with a diameter of nearly a full yard, one half of pure orihalcum and the opposite of pure starmetal. The two halves are not linearly bisected, but rather twined together like a rising flame and descending fang. The haft is white jade, twice as thick as a man\u2019s arm with hand-holds spaced regularly along its ten foot length. Two hearthstone slots are available on opposite sides of the sphere, both embedded in one pure metal.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of Shieldbreaker</b><br /> When a Solar, Sidereal or Getimian attunes to Shieldbreaker, she may use the Smashing gambit without paying the initiative cost, and increases the bonus for clash attacks to +5 instead of +3.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Weapon Shattering Strike</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m, 1i; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> Shieldbreaker is not idly named; the terrible strength of the weapon shatters swords and ruins shields. Weapon Shattering Strike enhances an attempt to disarm a mortal weapon. If the attempt is successful, the weapon is destroyed, although it may be repaired in time. <br /> <br /> At Essence 2, you may attempt to use Weapon Shattering Strike against an artifact weapon, but increase the difficulty of the gambit by the rating of the artifact.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Unstoppable Force</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 1wp; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Uniform<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Weapon Shattering Strike<br /> <br /> Sunlight and starlight stream from Shieldbreaker as it's bearer swings with a force that is impossible to deny. An attack enhanced with Unstoppable Force cannot be parried, and ignores defensive bonuses from light or heavy cover.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Fortress Leveling Blow</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> -; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Unstoppable Force<br /> <br /> Walls of stone and adamant cannot stand against the power of Shieldbreaker. So long as she is engaging in a destructive feat of strength with the weapon, the bearer of Shieldbreaker increases her Strength by 5.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Graceful Doom</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Unstoppable Force<br /> <br /> The force of Shieldbreaker moves the wielder as much as her victims. Upon using Graceful Doom to enhance a Rush, the bearer hurls the heavy weight of the weapon forward, reflexively moving her one range band in the direction of her target. If she flurries her rush with an attack, she may enhance the attack with Unstoppable Force for only 1 willpower.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Falling Star</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 7m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Graceful Doom<br /> <br /> The bearer swings Shieldbreaker into the air, allowing it to carry her upwards, only to come crashing down upon her enemies with a power of a falling star. This Charm enhances a decisive attack; if the attack hits, her victim is treated as having fallen a Medium distance (Exalted p. 232) and is knocked prone, as well as any damage they suffer from the strike itself. Falling Star may only be used once per scene, but is reset by reaching initiative 15+.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T11:28:11-07:00","id":921052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/920964-sidereal-wfhl-armed-and-armored-in-starlight-shieldbreaker#post920964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Evocations of Shieldbreaker</b><br /> When a Solar, Sidereal or Getimian attunes to Shieldbreaker, she may use the Smashing gambit without paying the initiative cost, and increases the bonus for clash attacks to +5 instead of +3.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Nononono.<br /> <br /> First, Smashing isn't a &quot;gambit&quot;, and it's already really good. Removing the Initiative cost isn't OP, I've done it before on Artifacts, but it's really good. Second, the two-handed bonus to clash is +2, not +3, and upgrading it to +5 means that when executing a clash attack, your super-hard-hitting heavy weapon has<i> higher accuracy than a light weapon</i>. No.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Weapon Shattering Strike</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m, 1i; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> Shieldbreaker is not idly named; the terrible strength of the weapon shatters swords and ruins shields. Weapon Shattering Strike enhances an attempt to disarm a mortal weapon. If the attempt is successful, the weapon is destroyed, although it may be repaired in time.<br /> <br /> At Essence 2, you may attempt to use Weapon Shattering Strike against an artifact weapon, but increase the difficulty of the gambit by the rating of the artifact. </div> </div> </div>Don't break people's Artifacts with a simple gambit that isn't even that hard to pull off. It's not cool. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Unstoppable Force</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 1wp; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Uniform<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Weapon Shattering Strike<br /> <br /> Sunlight and starlight stream from Shieldbreaker as it's bearer swings with a force that is impossible to deny. An attack enhanced with Unstoppable Force cannot be parried, and ignores defensive bonuses from light or heavy cover. </div> </div> </div>Why would you put an actual unblockable power as a simple 5m, 1wp effect with no other requirements or effects and no once/scene limit?<br /> <br /> If you're going to do this, make it part of a bigger effect, more expensive, and make it once/scene with a reset clause. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Fortress Leveling Blow</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> -; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Unstoppable Force<br /> <br /> Walls of stone and adamant cannot stand against the power of Shieldbreaker. So long as she is engaging in a destructive feat of strength with the weapon, the bearer of Shieldbreaker increases her Strength by 5. </div> </div> </div>I guess this is fine, but frankly a bit boring and cheap. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Graceful Doom</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Unstoppable Force<br /> <br /> The force of Shieldbreaker moves the wielder as much as her victims. Upon using Graceful Doom to enhance a Rush, the bearer hurls the heavy weight of the weapon forward, reflexively moving her one range band in the direction of her target. If she flurries her rush with an attack, she may enhance the attack with Unstoppable Force for only 1 willpower. </div> </div> </div>This makes Unstoppable Force even cheaper, so I have no need to tell you what I think of it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Falling Star</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 7m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Graceful Doom<br /> <br /> The bearer swings Shieldbreaker into the air, allowing it to carry her upwards, only to come crashing down upon her enemies with a power of a falling star. This Charm enhances a decisive attack; if the attack hits, her victim is treated as having fallen a Medium distance (Exalted p. 232) and is knocked prone, as well as any damage they suffer from the strike itself. Falling Star may only be used once per scene, but is reset by reaching initiative 15+. </div> </div> </div>This is <i>very </i>powerful. Probably fine for the final Evocation of an Artifact, I guess?<br /> <br /> Honestly I would rewrite this extensively. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T05:18:48-07:00","id":921444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/920964-sidereal-wfhl-armed-and-armored-in-starlight-shieldbreaker?p=921052#post921052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. Nononono.<br /> <br /> First, Smashing isn't a &quot;gambit&quot;, and it's already really good. Removing the Initiative cost isn't OP, I've done it before on Artifacts, but it's really good. Second, the two-handed bonus to clash is +2, not +3, and upgrading it to +5 means that when executing a clash attack, your super-hard-hitting heavy weapon has<i> higher accuracy than a light weapon</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bRe: Gambit.<br /> <br /> Fair enough; I'd contend it *should* be a gambit, because it's a special kind of attack that has a non-standard effect and gambits are made for that kind of bullshit, but it's not, so terminology error.<br /> <br /> Re: Clash bonus<br /> <br /> I'd meant for the clash bonus to be +2 over the normal two-handed bonus. I'd consider that on par with a general +1 to Accuracy- it's better in a strictly limited case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/920964-sidereal-wfhl-armed-and-armored-in-starlight-shieldbreaker?p=921052#post921052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No.<br /> Don't break people's Artifacts with a simple gambit that isn't even that hard to pull off. It's not cool.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted p. 200</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, remember that 7 successes on a decisive damage roll is normally enough to incapacitate or kill\u2014if your custom gambit is diffilty 7+, then its primary advantage over a normal decisive attack is going to be that it doesn\u2019t reset Initiative, unless it is custom-designed to be used against something with more than 7 Health Levels, like a behemoth.</div> </div> </div> </div>A difficulty 6 to 8 gambit isn't 'easy to pull off'- it's on the edge of 'this isn't worth doing', and makes damaging (and thus repairing) artifacts a thing that can happen, which makes crafting more valuable and interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/920964-sidereal-wfhl-armed-and-armored-in-starlight-shieldbreaker?p=921052#post921052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you put an actual unblockable power as a simple 5m, 1wp effect with no other requirements or effects and no once/scene limit?</div> </div> </div> </div>A lack of good benchmarking for unblockable effects?<br /> On the other hand, this should have some set up condition. I'll have to think about what would be interesting for such.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/920964-sidereal-wfhl-armed-and-armored-in-starlight-shieldbreaker?p=921052#post921052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is <i>very </i>powerful. Probably fine for the final Evocation of an Artifact, I guess?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've waffled between 'short' and 'medium' falling distance, drawing from Heaven Thunder Hammer. Given that this 7m has to be paid *before* the attack, an unconditional significant damage boost didn't seem that crazy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T07:09:24-07:00","id":921471,"title":"","content":"<b>Evocations of Shieldbreaker</b><br /> When a Solar, Sidereal or Getimian attunes to Shieldbreaker, she may make a Smashing attack without paying the initiative cost, and increases the bonus for clash attacks to +4 instead of +2.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Unstoppable Force</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 7m, 1wp; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Uniform<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Weapon Shattering Strike<br /> <br /> Sunlight and starlight stream from Shieldbreaker as it's bearer swings with a force that is impossible to deny. An attack enhanced with Unstoppable Force cannot be parried, and ignores defensive bonuses from light or heavy cover. Unstoppable Force can only be used in a turn after the bearer has advanced at least one or more range bands.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Graceful Doom</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 7m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Unstoppable Force<br /> <br /> The force of Shieldbreaker moves the wielder as much as her victims. Upon using Graceful Doom to enhance a Rush, the bearer hurls the heavy weight of the weapon forward, reflexively moving her one range band in the direction of her target. If she flurries her rush with an attack, she may enhance the attack with Unstoppable Force for only 2 motes and 1 willpower.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}